          "notes": [
            "Root independently read the complete official Chinese Programs page, including both separately headed Long-term Chinese Program and Short-term Chinese Program entries. The selected short-term entry explicitly recruits Foreigners, requires the foreign-student application form for Shanghai Ocean University and describes Chinese-language curricula. It is a concrete language-training programme, not an unspecified admission entry or a degree major.",
            "All six existing raw Shanghai Ocean identities, complete current binding namespace and historical target identities were read. The existing long-term Chinese-language record points to this same URL. That unchanged record denotes semester-based long-term study with its own curriculum and level objectives. The separately named short-term programme offers on-demand short-course and tutorial formats with its own entry conditions and language/cultural curriculum. This is a genuinely different official category, not merely a different annual application round of the long-term entry.",
            "Summer and winter starts, week/month options, one-on-one formats and elective themes remain inside this single short-term programme; none becomes another identity. The old bachelor-applicant Chinese preparatory route is a different foundation purpose, not this open short-course language entry. Aquaculture, Marine Science and Food Science degree identities remain unchanged. No long-term alias is stripped or approved and no unsupported scan/OCR source is used.",
            "The full official main-site HTML was normally captured with verified TLS, public DNS and robots handling. The programme-specific name/international quote is taken from the short-term body heading, not its menu link. The degree-category quote is the same short-term section Chinese Language Programs curriculum, and the institution quote is its own filled-application-form condition.",
            "The footer copyright2015 does not establish the intake year, so sourceDeclaredYear is null. Historical fees, registration charges, durations, seasonal dates, age conditions, housing, optional activities and teaching arrangements remain unapproved context. Only one source-English language directory identity is approved; no Chinese/Russian translation, scholarship, current opportunity or full school catalogue reconciliation is inferred."
